#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078264 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078398 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e360e71d-82f6-5226-af82-bfc4d0e5363d" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Reciprocal Trigonometric Ratios Given a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "4f967310-913e-5082-ab9b-87b1eceb3ddb" :question/math-academy-id "e-3258" :question/problem "Find $\\csc\\theta,$ $\\sec\\theta,$ and $\\cot\\theta$ for the triangle below.\n\n![](images/34/343917ea041d51cac38619f3577765eee7fbc3ea85e175148b6c591e11ae230b.png)" :question/worked-solution "We compute the three reciprocal trigonometric ratios as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\csc\\theta &= \\dfrac{1}{\\sin\\theta} = \\dfrac {\\text{hypotenuse}} {\\text{opposite}} = \\dfrac 5 3, \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\sec\\theta &= \\dfrac{1}{\\cos\\theta} =  \\dfrac {\\text{hypotenuse}} {\\text{adjacent}} = \\dfrac 5 4, \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\cot\\theta &= \\dfrac{1}{\\tan\\theta} = \\dfrac {\\text{adjacent}} {\\text{opposite}} = \\dfrac 4 3.\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078265 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078399 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8659f97-a242-543f-9668-f547ca1f4d95" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Reciprocal Trigonometric Ratio Given a Triangle Using the Pythagorean Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "d2f40096-4001-5cd9-aeda-52c5894649b4" :question/math-academy-id "e-3261" :question/problem "Find $\\sec L$ for $\\triangle KLJ$ (shown below).\n\n![](images/c0/c08613b38502628d71ffa0cdac65400420fb25926a64b747b925ee06d6d560ca.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that $\\sec$ is the reciprocal of $\\cos.$ So first we need to compute cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos L = \\dfrac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} = \\dfrac{JL}{KL} = \\dfrac{JL}{5}\n$$\n\nTo find the length $JL,$ we can use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}JL & =\\sqrt{K{L}^{2}-J{K}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}-{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25-9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\cos L = \\dfrac{JL}{5} = \\dfrac{4}{5},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡L & ={(\\frac{4}{5})}^{-1}=\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540074 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078399 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8659f97-a242-543f-9668-f547ca1f4d95" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Reciprocal Trigonometric Ratio Given a Triangle Using the Pythagorean Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f66b5f8-e76f-5f77-8f96-098a448df87a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539542} {:answer/id #uuid "22e0ee74-658c-52fe-a2b1-2df54d380881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539547} {:answer/id #uuid "38ae8a7e-8879-58a2-b77d-2f1efa7ea909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539585} {:answer/id #uuid "9579f35d-0a62-56c0-87be-1dce6c45f688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539727} {:answer/id #uuid "fdf065d6-21d7-507f-b607-cc7b49b70a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9579f35d-0a62-56c0-87be-1dce6c45f688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539727} :answer-field/id #uuid "42169019-4c90-5f92-9ed4-0e9272ff36d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9728a2a0-30c7-53d5-836b-39033ca5b896" :question/math-academy-id "q-122902" :question/problem "![](images/a9/a9003434f721485b5ee3eb2ed417d0c4c68514b98060f6149bc974270e55411a.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{csc}⁡P=$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that $csc$ is the reciprocal of $sin.$ So first we need to compute sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡P=\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}=\\frac{QR}{PR}=\\frac{QR}{15}\n$$\n\nTo find the length $QR,$ we can use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}QR & =\\sqrt{P{R}^{2}-P{Q}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{15}^{2}-{9}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{225-81} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144} \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡P=\\frac{QR}{15}=\\frac{12}{15}=\\frac{4}{5},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡P={(\\frac{4}{5})}^{-1}=\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540049 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078398 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e360e71d-82f6-5226-af82-bfc4d0e5363d" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Reciprocal Trigonometric Ratios Given a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01908de7-7512-523d-ba70-c9c1a7ef7124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{113}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539479} {:answer/id #uuid "115431ac-729e-5559-8a56-b1f21dcbb60c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{113}{112}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539511} {:answer/id #uuid "a41e199f-ca14-5113-b9c2-b8e50141ee9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{112}{113}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539755} {:answer/id #uuid "a7962394-8ee4-5282-84a9-dbe8bf1bb6f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{112}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539761} {:answer/id #uuid "b523e18b-4f49-563f-b5f9-5857eb37fb10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{112}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b523e18b-4f49-563f-b5f9-5857eb37fb10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{112}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539792} :answer-field/id #uuid "12f70ae7-825b-51a0-9a22-13ca854d1af0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4bfcc405-f2a2-5e8e-bff5-6d6acca08903" :question/math-academy-id "q-25070" :question/problem "![](images/6e/6eda76bbacb2cbebfe9a798b957c013dc34f684b4d866488541af759b25972b7.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{cot}⁡D=$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the cotangent of the angle $D$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡D=\\frac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{opposite}}=\\frac{15}{112}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540101 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078398 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e360e71d-82f6-5226-af82-bfc4d0e5363d" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Reciprocal Trigonometric Ratios Given a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18751d4d-66c7-55dd-ab9d-0457e8043e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539529} {:answer/id #uuid "4d9fcc09-b9d2-53dc-ba2d-c997dd3c5612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539618} {:answer/id #uuid "6f61adb7-252c-5012-8cfe-25791dae6092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539666} {:answer/id #uuid "710fafca-d907-583c-aeec-b6987c81b2bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539670} {:answer/id #uuid "efa0d994-cbc3-50ba-9bbb-a1a4704fc3ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18751d4d-66c7-55dd-ab9d-0457e8043e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539529} :answer-field/id #uuid "024c165a-c9fd-50e0-9cfb-6a88ae65e64f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de4398c2-dc93-57fc-955e-876f667d9e66" :question/math-academy-id "q-4650" :question/problem "![](images/7f/7f566dccaab9ea71af6fa627ce53bd400e97735d5b8c7500d63fddfdf2e7a8db.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{sec}⁡R=$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the secant of the angle $R$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡R=\\frac{\\text{hypotenuse}}{\\text{adjacent}}=\\frac{10}{6}=\\frac{5}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078399 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8659f97-a242-543f-9668-f547ca1f4d95" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Reciprocal Trigonometric Ratio Given a Triangle Using the Pythagorean Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58e41124-d27e-5bf8-a849-55991f19b628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539631} {:answer/id #uuid "b1098335-0f3d-532a-9ba1-59d86a55f4e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539778} {:answer/id #uuid "bd65e325-f1b8-5c87-9662-6c18254e66f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539807} {:answer/id #uuid "f74d244e-220f-5aa8-ba66-446e22db924d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539897} {:answer/id #uuid "fadee215-c360-5052-9061-2ac46dc7f6ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58e41124-d27e-5bf8-a849-55991f19b628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539631} :answer-field/id #uuid "db152ebb-c302-5112-8c45-9948cd14ca8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "789a361b-1deb-51ca-88a0-26707116d922" :question/math-academy-id "q-65381" :question/problem "![](images/e9/e980e9415d52338c90eb5c167a32b02815237b1554f9aea06f831e88db6f3777.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that $cot$ is the reciprocal of $tan.$ So first we need to compute tangent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}}=\\frac{PR}{QR}=\\frac{3}{QR}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the length $QR,$ we can use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}QR & =\\sqrt{P{Q}^{2}-P{R}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3\\sqrt{5})^{2}-{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{45-9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{6}=\\frac{1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-1}=2.\n$$"}]}
